== 3. The 3-adic visit law of T_+: stationary law of the fair-coin chain mod 3^m
   mod 3 (exact): 1: 1/3, 2: 2/3
   mod 9 (exact): 1: 8/63, 2: 16/63, 4: 11/63, 5: 4/63, 7: 2/63, 8: 22/63
   mod 3^1: support 2 of 3;  entropy of the new digit 0.5794 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.6667, worst 0.6667
   mod 3^2: support 6 of 9;  entropy of the new digit 0.8468 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.4762, worst 0.4762
   mod 3^3: support 18 of 27;  entropy of the new digit 0.8981 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.4057, worst 0.4377
   mod 3^4: support 54 of 81;  entropy of the new digit 0.9258 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.3425, worst 0.4276
   mod 3^5: support 162 of 243;  entropy of the new digit 0.9437 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.2972, worst 0.4216
   mod 3^6: support 486 of 729;  entropy of the new digit 0.9552 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.2627, worst 0.4186
   mod 3^7: support 1458 of 2187;  entropy of the new digit 0.9635 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.2349, worst 0.4164
   mod 3^8: support 4374 of 6561;  entropy of the new digit 0.9695 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.2127, worst 0.4154
   mod 3^9: support 13122 of 19683;  entropy of the new digit 0.9742 (log 3 = 1);  top digit given the lower ones: mass-weighted L1 deviation 0.1942, worst 0.4147
   reading: biased at the coarse 3-adic scale (1/3 : 2/3 mod 3); finer digits approach uniformity on average (conditional entropy rises toward 1, the mean deviation decays slowly), not at every residue (the worst stays near 0.41)

